# desert_rock.fmat — the rock effects, as a worked example
# (docs/guide/28-materials.md, docs/canyon/PHASE_5.md).
#
# `rock` projected TRIPLANAR (world space, upright, no UVs needed — what a
# generated rock or a cliff wants), regraded toward the red of sandstone
# country, with dark desert-varnish streaks down its steep faces, slow macro
# variation to break the repeat, and close-up grain from `stone_floor`'s
# normal map.
kind: surface
texture: rock
doc: Red desert rock, triplanar, varnished. Put it on anything with no useful UVs.
effects:
  - effect: triplanar
    scale: 2.5
  - effect: color_grade
    match: 0.6
    target: [0.62, 0.38, 0.27]
  - effect: streaks
    strength: 0.45
  - effect: macro_variation
    scale: 20
  - effect: detail_normal
    map: stone_floor
    scale: 0.4
